  "door_slot_s": 8,
  "door_offset_from_carry_start_s": 40,
  "door_rule": "The 8-second exclusive interval is included in 110-second carry. FCFS, ties r1 first; queue delay shifts the remaining carry and release. Return occupies an 8-second slot starting 32 seconds into its 88 seconds; no return/outbound overlap occurs in these selected schedules.",
  "message_s": 2,
  "oracle_messages": 0,
  "upper_definition": "Performance upper bound: maximize capped correct demand, then minimize full-demand makespan in this declared model. Not a measured physical minimum.",
  "baseline_definition": "A fixed local T0 policy, not a universal mathematical lower bound. Scan for 12s. If no known orders, abstain until deadline. Otherwise select lowest-ID unfinished known order, then nearest observed matching box (ties visual left-to-right); mark own delivery only. If another known order remains, return for 88s and survey for 12s; take next visible matching box for 58s, or stop if none remains. Never collect already-delivered boxes from the destination room. No shared completion feedback, no inference from another robot's route.",
  "count_rule": "Sum min(required count, correctly delivered count) independently for each colour/sign pair; surplus deliveries score zero. Wrong deliveries do not subtract points.",
  "time_rule": "policy_active_end_s excludes idle uninformed robots; full_completion_s is null if demand remains unmet at 900s. Capped completion is then 900, not active termination.",
  "selection_rule": "Reject iff correct counts equal AND (baseline capped completion - oracle completion)/oracle completion < 0.20.",
  "minimality_certificate": "Two-order scenes: each initial pickup is at least 58s, so earliest door entry is110 and second door entry118 (exit126); finishing second delivery requires80s after entry (72s after exit), giving198s. One-near-box-per-robot attains198. Any serial two-delivery plan needs at least12+58+110+10+88+12+58+110+10=468s, hence cannot win. Single-order decoy scenes: enumerate both robots; robot r2 is nearest to the required-colour target and minimizes12+72.5*d+110+10 with no competing traffic. Nonordered boxes cannot improve completion.",
